The sharpest V2 finding so far is that it is not simply “newer V1”: V2 has durable SQLite/event-log semantics and staged undo, but sharing and LSP are explicitly non-functional, and the beta client still leaves reconnect policy to callers. I’m now grounding every “we have/we lack” comparison in `origin/main` searches, including negative claims.
