   360	
   361	## 5. Key algorithms
   362	
   363	### 5.1 Manifest scan
   364	
   365	`scanBoringPlugins(pluginDirs)` discovers plugin package roots, validates
   366	manifest shape, resolves contained entry paths, detects duplicate ids, and
   367	returns `BoringServerPluginManifest[]` plus preflight diagnostics.
   368	
   369	### 5.2 Signatures and revisions
   370	
   371	`BoringPluginAssetManager` hashes manifest fields, front/server file
   372	signatures, relevant front/server/shared directories, and Pi resource paths.
   373	When a signature changes, the plugin revision increments and a load/unload/error
   374	event is emitted.
   375	
   376	### 5.3 Front import cache busting
   377	
   378	Browser imports append both revision and salt:
   379	
   380	```ts
   381	import(`${frontUrl}?v=${revision}&t=${Date.now()}`)
   382	```
   383	
   384	The salt avoids stale Vite/browser module graph reuse across repeated reloads
   385	or dev-server restarts.
   386	
   387	### 5.4 Atomic registry replacement
   388	
   389	Front factories are first captured into an in-memory API. The captured panels,
   390	commands, catalogs, and surface resolvers are then installed with
   391	`replaceByPluginId` per registry. DockView and registry subscribers should not
   392	see an intermediate empty state.
   393	
   394	### 5.5 Server drift warnings
   395	
   396	When a plugin had a server entry in a previous revision and that server file
   397	changes, the load event carries `requiresRestart: ["routes", "agentTools"]`.
   398	The chat reload response also includes restart warnings so users know `/reload`
   399	updated front/Pi resources but not boot-wired server code.
   400	
   401	### 5.6 Path containment
   402	
   403	Manifest paths are lexically safe relative paths and are checked with realpath
   404	containment so symlink escapes are rejected. Runtime workspace provisioning
   405	template targets are also constrained to remain inside the workspace root.
   406	
   407	### 5.7 Output ownership and collision detection
   408	
   409	Plugin-owned outputs carry `pluginId`. Hot reload uses that ownership to replace
   410	only the current plugin's outputs. Cross-plugin id collisions are rejected with
   411	`PLUGIN_OUTPUT_ID_COLLISION`; intra-plugin duplicate output ids are rejected
   412	while capturing the front factory.
   413	
